From: afni-win
Subject: [PATCH] thd_getpathprogs: find executables with an .exe suffix on Windows

Why the compat layer cannot handle this: THD_find_executable() lists the
executable files in every PATH directory and compares their names with the
requested name exactly ("gzip"). On Windows the file is "gzip.exe", so the
lookup never succeeds; thd_compress.c then marks gzip/bzip2 as missing and
AFNI_COMPRESSOR=GZIP silently writes uncompressed .BRIK files, and the
same lookup is used for curl/wget and other helper programs. The comparison
happens inside upstream code on directory listings, so no replacement header
or library function can change it. Under _WIN32 the patch also accepts the
requested name followed by ".exe" (case-insensitive suffix).

diff --git a/src/thd_getpathprogs.c b/src/thd_getpathprogs.c
index 678558e..e67cea8 100644
--- a/src/thd_getpathprogs.c
+++ b/src/thd_getpathprogs.c
@@ -38,6 +38,12 @@ ENTRY("THD_find_executable") ;
    for( ii=0 ; ii < elist->num ; ii++ ){
       str = THD_trailname( elist->ar[ii] , 0 ) ;
       if( strcmp(str,etr) == 0 ) RETURN(elist->ar[ii]) ;
+#ifdef _WIN32
+      /* executables carry a ".exe" suffix on Windows [afni-win] */
+      { size_t ll = strlen(etr) ;
+        if( strncmp(str,etr,ll) == 0 && strcasecmp(str+ll,".exe") == 0 )
+          RETURN(elist->ar[ii]) ; }
+#endif
    }
 
    RETURN(NULL) ;
